{
  "dom_id": "step-q118657",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Each side of a cubic room has length $\\frac{7}{2}\\,\\text{yd}.$ What is the volume of the room?",
  "worked_solution": "We need to find the volume of a cube.\n\nThe volume $V$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=\\frac{7}{2}\\,\\text{yd}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nV={(\\frac{7}{2}\\,\\text{yd})}^{3}=\\frac{343}{8}\\,{\\text{yd}}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the room is $\\frac{343}{8}\\,{\\text{yd}}^{3}.$",
